 In that case, set `SERVICE_WORKER_CORS_ENABLED=false` so the service worker fetches uploaded files without CORS mode.
 
+#### Push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can send web push notifications to phones and desktops for everything that lands in someone's notification tray.
+People turn them on for each device from their Notification Settings.
+
+To enable them, set a VAPID key pair. You can generate one with:
+
+```sh
+docker run --rm ghcr.io/basecamp/fizzy:main bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}", "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+```
+
+- `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY`
+- `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY`
+
+Keep the pair stable: browsers bind their subscriptions to the public key, so changing it means everyone has to turn push notifications on again.
+Push notifications need your instance to be served over HTTPS (see `BASE_URL`).
+
 #### Multi-tenant mode
 
 By default, when you run the Fizzy Docker image you'll be limited to creating a single account (although that account can have as many users as you like).
